# A delete leaves a Tombstone; every later CMS Event for that id is SkippedDeleted.
@run = 1
@id = delete-{{run}}
@unknownId = never-seen-{{run}}

### Publish v1
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Short-lived" } }
]

### One Batch: delete, then publish v2 later: delete applies, publish SkippedDeleted
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "delete", "id": "{{id}}", "timestamp": "2026-01-01T11:00:00Z" },
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 2, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T11:05:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Back?" } }
]

### Admin: 404, deleted is gone for everyone
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### Much later publish v9: SkippedDeleted, the Tombstone is final
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 9, "timestamp": "2026-06-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Resurrected?" } }
]

### Admin: still 404
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### Delete of an id never seen: SkippedUnknown
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "delete", "id": "{{unknownId}}", "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z" }
]
